    {
      "id": "glass_taj_metered_told",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“Every well.” A beat, and then, because he cannot help it: “There is one that is not a well. The bath under the Glass Quarter has never been metered, not once, not in the whole run of the boards.” He straightens a board that did not need it. “It is not a well, so it is not mine. That is the position.”"
        }
      ],
      "onEnter": [
        {
          "learnLore": {
            "entry": "glass_bath_metered"
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "glass_taj_metered_on",
          "text": "Go on.",
          "goto": "greet",
          "effects": [],
          "onceOnly": false,
          "showWhenLocked": false,
          "lockedHint": ""
        }
      ],
      "redirectWhen": []
    },
    {
      "id": "glass_taj_metered_wont",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“I've said all I mean to,” they say, and go back to what they were doing."
        }
      ],
      "onEnter": [
        {
          "adjustReputation": {
            "faction": "the_water_wardens",
            "amount": -1
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "glass_taj_metered_drop",
          "text": "Leave it.",
          "goto": "greet",
          "effects": [],
          "onceOnly": false,
          "showWhenLocked": false,
          "lockedHint": ""
        }
      ],
      "redirectWhen": []
    },
    {
      "id": "glass_taj_nine_told",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“Nine.” He does not have to look it up. “Which has been irritating me since I took the boards, because Saltrun cuts eight and everyone on that coast cuts eight, and the returns have said nine for two hundred years.” He shrugs, very slightly. “It is salt, not water. Not mine.”"
        }
      ],
      "onEnter": [
